rk Times Company, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 14 Nov 2013:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(attributive) Of, by, relating to, or belonging to an enemy.", "tags": ["attributive"], "examples": ["The building was destroyed by enemy bombing."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(video games) A non-player character that tries to harm the player.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Use gadgets like Nakishkas to fend off enemies.", "reference": "2008, “Story Mode”, in Cory in the House: Instruction Booklet, Burbank, California: Disney Interactive Studios; Nintendo, page 8:"}], "synonyms": ["mob"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["adversary", "antagonist", "backfriend", "bane", "bête noire", "corrival", "enemy", "fiend", "foe", "foeman", "unfriend", "nemesis", "opponent", "opposer", "rival"], "antonyms": ["accomplice", "ally", "friend", "pal", "partner", "supporter"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɛnəmi/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈenəmi/", "tags": ["General Australian", "New Zealand"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɛnəme/", "tags": ["Scotland"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/-mɪ/", "tags": ["Scotland"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/-mi/", "tags": ["Scotland"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈɛnɪmi/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "enemies", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "enemying", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "enemied", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "enemied", "tags": ["past"]}, {"word": "enemie", "tags": ["alternative", "obsolete"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To make an enemy of.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "These prelates and nobles, seeing themselves dispossessed by the death of 